// 1. PROFILE: async-profiler (CPU + alloc flame graphs) or JFR.
// 3. ONE CHANGE at the measured hotspot. The Scala/JVM wins:

//    a. boxing: List[Double]/Vector[Double] box each element (a pointer chase);
//       Array[Double] is a primitive array and streams.
val xs: Array[Double] = new Array[Double](n)
var s = 0.0
var i = 0
while (i < xs.length) { s += xs(i); i += 1 }   // indexed loop over a primitive array

//    b. collection overhead: List/Vector operations cost per element; a plain
//       Array loop is the fast path when the collection API is not needed.

//    c. a case class in a hot loop allocates unless the collection is
//       primitive-specialised.

